@34 = ~What are you doing in my house! Get out or I shall call the Flaming Fist!~
@35 = ~Forgive us. Wrong house.~
@36 = ~We are here to end your miserable life. Astarion's regards.~
@37 = ~We are here to warn you. A vampire called Astarion wants you dead. He sent us to commit the deed, but we refuse to do so.~
@38 = ~Oh no. Astarion? I don't have much time. I... I need to get out of here. I need to leave the city immediately before they kill me. I... thank you for telling me. I don't have much but... please take this. I won't give you more because I need money for my travels. Long... travels.~
@39 = ~Keep your gold. Get out of Baldur's Gate and don't look back.~
@40 = ~What did you do to deserve their hatred toward you?~
@41 = ~Wait… if we don't bring him your body, we won't get our reward. I am not willing to part with gold.~
@42 = ~I changed my mind. I'll kill you. Nothing personal.~
@43 = ~You... you're serious? After coming here with orders to kill me, you're simply letting me go? Then perhaps there is still some decency left in this cursed city. Thank you. I shall leave immediately. May whatever gods you worship watch over you.~
@44 = ~Please. I cannot offer you six thousand gold. But I can offer you everything I have here. Take it and leave me alive. I promise I will never return. Tell Astarion that I ran before you could reach me.~
@45 = ~You bastard! You won't get me without a fight!~
@46 = ~I gambled with a powerful vampire lord - Cazador without realising it. I lost my fortune to him. We had a bet going on. If he wins, he can kill me. If I win, he will transform me into a vampire so I can be immortal. I lost the bet, and wasn't ready for consequences. I panicked, and bolted it out of there. He has been hunting me ever since however and sending his minions to find me. I evaded him but I knew I can't do it forever and... here we are. I blame my own stupidity for attempting to make a bargain with a vampire lord.~
